220
00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:56.073
and then be very upset about the disapproval.

221
00:09:57.870 --> 00:09:59.100
So it's a quite different state.

222
00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:02.730
Like you could be an introvert and not be shy or vice versa.

223
00:10:02.730 --> 00:10:06.450
But my work, I would say focuses on both,

224
00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:07.320
both ways of being,

225
00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:11.130
because both ways of being show up very similarly

226
00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:12.690
in terms of behavior.

227
00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:15.090
And so they get judged in similar ways.

228
00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:16.230
Right, right.

229
00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:19.380
And shyness being something that is mutable,

230
00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:22.860
but perhaps introversion or extroversion is more

231
00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:24.450
fundamental or constitution.

232
00:10:24.450 --> 00:10:26.550
Like is there immutability to it?

233
00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:27.717
Yeah, I don't know if I'd say that

